<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="229" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Cost model for dedicated stamps: no shared-trial tier, the H0 cost envelope binds every model (tier + estimate required at intake, no warnAndProceed), one H13 envelope for an empty customer stamp re-derived from current prices</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T229 (G4, G13)</phase>
    <gate>after 228 (✅)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>L2 API intake validation + H0/H13 code and options, intake schema, operator skill, binding docs; tests modified.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting provisioning-contract change (API, handlers, schema, skill) with a cost-control invariant.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits the provision-environment skill and .claude/constraints (main-session-only).</parallel-reason>
    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, l2-controlplane, model1-dedicated, cost, testing</tags>
    <deps>228</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make the provisioning cost model match D-12: every customer gets a dedicated stamp (Model 1 paid by Spaarke, Model 2 by the customer), so no shared-tier cost concept may remain.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, intake contract, operator skill).</role>

  <goal>
    The cost gates assume one thing: a run deploys one full customer stamp (customer.bicep) into the customer's own
    subscription. H0 refuses any run whose operator-declared monthly estimate exceeds its tier ceiling, for every model,
    with no override; H13 compares the measured subscription cost with ONE envelope for an empty stamp (spec §15 #14:
    "one envelope per customer covering the full dedicated stamp, in both models … re-derive the number against current
    Azure pricing").
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Mapped 2026-10-06. `tier` (shared-trial | smb | enterprise | dedicated) is read only by H0's cost gate. H0 fails
      closed on missing/unknown inputs only for Model 2 (`RequireCostEnvelopeForModel2Dedicated`, `isModel2Dedicated`) and
      allows `costEnvelopePolicy = warnAndProceed` — "Model 1 shared-trial ONLY" — for Model 1. Model 1 is now a Spaarke-paid
      dedicated stamp, so the reason Model 2 barred an uncapped budget (an overrun wastes real money before H13 can see it)
      applies to both models and no permitted case for warnAndProceed remains. The skill's interactive mode collects neither
      tier nor estimate and offers a client-only "Proceed anyway?" that H0 then contradicts.
      H13: `Model1MarginalEnvelopeUsd` (430, "marginal on a shared platform") and `Model2EmptyEnvelopeUsd` (400) — both models
      deploy the same customer.bicep since D19, and since T228 the query scope (the customer's subscription) holds exactly
      one stamp.
      Re-derived 2026-10-06 from the Azure Retail Prices API (westus2, 730 h): App Service S1 Linux $58.40, AI Search
      Standard S1 (1×1) $245.28, Managed Redis Balanced B0 with high availability (2 × $0.016/h) $23.36, Service Bus Standard
      base $10.00 = $337.04 fixed; Cosmos serverless, Storage, Key Vault, Log Analytics/App Insights, OpenAI, Document
      Intelligence and Content Safety are consumption-billed (near zero for an empty stamp). Envelope $400 stands, now
      derived.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/Preflight/{H0Options,H0PreflightHandler}.cs; Core/Modules/HandlersModule.cs</file>
      <file>Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/{H13AcceptanceOptions,ArmCostEnvelopeChecker}.cs</file>
      <file>Api/Api/{RunsEndpoints,ControlPlaneProblems}.cs; Core/Models/IntakeParameterCatalog.cs; Core/Reconciler/HandlerRunInputs.cs</file>
      <file>scripts/provisioning-prereqs/intake.schema.json; .claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md (Step 1.0 batch loader, Step 1 interactive, Step 2 BAT-10, Step 4.0 payload)</file>
      <file>spec.md NFR-04 + §15 #14; docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md; BFF Services/Ai/Metering XML docs (stale "shared trial/SMB" rationale)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-12">No shared-tier cost concept anywhere (tier, envelope, policy text) in src, scripts, the schema or the skill.</constraint>
    <constraint source="needed-or-remove">`warnAndProceed` has no permitted case → `costEnvelopePolicy` goes (schema, catalog, H0, skill). `RequireCostEnvelopeForModel2Dedicated` / `isModel2Dedicated` go — the inputs are required for every model at intake and H0 fails closed on them while the gate is on (`CostEnvelopeAbortsPreflight` stays the one switch).</constraint>
    <constraint source="parity">The intake schema and POST /api/runs agree: `tier` (smb | enterprise | dedicated) and `estimatedMonthlyUsd` (invariant decimal ≥ 0) are required by both; the schema's tier enum equals H0's built-in ceiling table.</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF">BFF changes are XML-doc text only (no code); state it — no publish-size measurement needed for comment-only edits.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests">Hand-written fakes; never Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Intake: schema (tier enum without shared-trial; tier + estimatedMonthlyUsd required; costEnvelopePolicy removed; examples), catalog, POST /api/runs validation + problem codes, H0 run inputs; parity tests.</step>
    <step order="2">H0: one decision path for every model (missing / unknown / unparseable → Resumable refusal; over ceiling → quota-cost-overrun); remove the policy branch and the Model 2 option; tests.</step>
    <step order="3">H13: one `DedicatedStampEnvelopeUsd` (400, derivation in its doc comment); the checker stops selecting by model; tests.</step>
    <step order="4">Skill: interactive prompts for tier + estimate (with the empty-stamp floor as guidance); batch loader requires them; Step 2 overrun is a hard stop in both modes; payload without costEnvelopePolicy.</step>
    <step order="5">Docs: spec NFR-04 + §15 #14, guide, constraints, BFF metering XML docs, plan G4/G13, CHANGELOG.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify (ControlPlane tests, ArchTests, Worker + Api builds 0 warnings); Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/runs returns 400 for a request without `tier`, with an unknown tier (incl. `shared-trial`), without `estimatedMonthlyUsd`, or with a negative / non-decimal estimate; schema and endpoint agree (parity test); the schema's tier enum equals `H0Options.DefaultCeilingsUsd` keys.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H0, gate on, for Model 1 AND Model 2: missing tier / unknown tier / missing estimate / unparseable estimate → Resumable refusal; estimate over ceiling → `quota-cost-overrun` whatever else the run carries; under → pass. Gate off → skip.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H13 expects the same envelope for Model 1 and Model 2.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git grep -i` finds no `shared-trial`, `warnAndProceed`, `costEnvelopePolicy`, `Model1MarginalEnvelope`, `Model2EmptyEnvelope`, `RequireCostEnvelopeForModel2Dedicated` in src, scripts or the skill (history notes excepted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane.Tests and ArchTests pass; Worker/Api build with 0 warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Something other than H0 reads `tier` or `costEnvelopePolicy`.</trigger>
    <trigger>A budget amount has to be chosen (e.g. a per-customer OpenAI cap) — that is the owner's number.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-10-06 (SESSION 40).
    - New Core/Handlers/Preflight/CostEnvelopeIntake (static, UserProvisioningIntake pattern): tier ∈ smb | enterprise |
      dedicated (= H0Options.DefaultCeilingsUsd keys, exact case) and estimatedMonthlyUsd = digits with an optional '.'
      between digits (exactly the skill's ^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$). POST /api/runs (ValidateOperatorIntake) and H0 call it;
      codes quota-cost-envelope-required-missing / -unknown-tier / -unparseable-estimate. Schema: both required, tier enum
      without shared-trial, costEnvelopePolicy removed (now an unknown key → 400); catalog + HandlerRunInputs (required).
    - H0: one path for every model — unusable input → Resumable refusal; over ceiling → quota-cost-overrun; no waiver.
      Removed: costEnvelopePolicy / warnAndProceed constants + branch, RequireCostEnvelopeForModel2Dedicated, isModel2Dedicated,
      shared-trial ceiling (−203 lines). H0Options.Validate() + ValidateOnStart: a configured ceiling for a tier intake
      refuses (e.g. a leftover shared-trial setting) or a non-positive one fails the Worker at startup. Overrun message:
      the remedy is a NEW run (intake is fixed at POST), invariant-culture amounts.
    - H13: one H13AcceptanceOptions.DedicatedStampEnvelopeUsd = 400 for every model (SelectExpectedEnvelope removed);
      re-derived from the Azure Retail Prices API 2026-10-06 (westus2, 730 h): App Service S1 Linux 58.40 + AI Search S1
      245.28 + Managed Redis B0 HA 23.36 + Service Bus Standard 10.00 = 337.04 fixed; the rest consumption-billed.
      Validate() refuses a non-positive envelope (would make the drift check always pass). Doc notes the two-sided drift.
    - Skill: Step 1b-ter (prompts + validation, floor guidance), batch loader without costEnvelopePolicy, Step 2 overrun is a
      hard stop in both modes (built-in ceilings; note to mirror any configured ceiling), Step 4.0 requires + sends both
      ([decimal]→invariant string, no exponent), sample outputs without the $430 marginal envelope.
    - Docs: guide §3.2 cost + new §3.2a, H0/H13 rows (H0 row also lost T228's stale "env-creation rate"), H13 criteria;
      constraints new binding "Cost model" section; spec NFR-04 + §15 #14 (re-derived ✅); design §14 superseded note;
